  "# Codegen co-scientist, iteration 9

WIP=1 is still closing the LLVM gap on `kernel_wide`. Iteration 6 moved the
pool. Iteration 7 is Belady spill placement. Iteration 8 measured the
call/all-vreg hole and is not this file. Encode-time MADD after the leaf
cache (kotoba-native `c55711d`) turned eight offset lanes into eight MADDs.
LLVM does not do that.

## What LLVM actually emits

AArch64 rustc -O3, scalar, no NEON. The kernel is inlined into the 100k loop.
Round 1 is **one** `mul x14, n, #48271` and then `add` of precomputed
`(k*48271+1)`. Round 2 is eight `madd`. Remainder is already a Mersenne
sequence. Dump: `/tmp/kernel-wide-dump-260818/`.

`(n+k)*C+1` is `n*C+(k*C+1)` in wrapping i64. Eight lanes share `n*C`.

## The change

A GMIR pass at the end of `lower-kir-expression`:

1. Distribute `mul (add x k) C` → `add (mul x C) (k*C)` when k and C are i64
   constants. Commutative in both operators. The add that produced `n+k` stays
   if it still has other readers.
2. Fold `add (add x a) b` → `add x (a+b)` when a and b are const, so the
   trailing `+1` becomes the addend `k*C+1`.
3. GVN identical `mul x C` within a basic block. No move.
4. DCE only unused `:gmir/constant` and `:gmir/add`. Quotient stays even when
   unread (ordered `do` still has to trap).

AArch64 fusion grew a unique-use check. After CSE, one mul has eight add
users. Fusing the first would drop the mul while the other seven still read
it. Count uses of the product **until that register is killed**. Counting to
the end of the function treats a later live-range of the same physical as a
use of this product, and that refusal broke the already-landed
`(+ (* n 7) 1)` then `(- v (* n 3))` MADD/MSUB pair.

Landed: kotoba-native `c15026ff` (merge of `agent/offset-mul-reassoc`).
West pin `314f9be9` → `c15026ff` (superproject `8d7a0827`). Do not bump amu
without perfgate.

## Break / unbreak

Eight-lane first-round without the rewrite: 8 independent muls, or 8 madds
after the cache. With it: GMIR has **one** `:gmir/multiply` whose non-constant
operand is the argument. Encoded bytes: **1 MUL, 0 MADD** on that form.
`kernel_wide`: **1 MUL + 8 MADD**. Fusion of a reused product refuses
(lower-mc unit test, two add users). Wrapping identity: `2*Long/MAX_VALUE`
is the i64 `-2`, not a BigInt. Full suite: 165 tests, 2185 assertions.

The leaf-cache test that used `(+ n 7)` then `(* a 7)` then `(+ b 7)` is no
longer that program — it is `n*7+56`. Three uses of 7 moved to bit-and/or/xor.

## Honest leftover

Even with round 1 = 1 mul + 8 adds:

- Fuel-on-entry remains.
- LLVM still inlines into the timed loop; amu still calls a function pointer
  (`kexe-benchmark`).
- The call / all-vreg path is unchanged (iteration 8 named it; this pass does
  not touch it).
- Seal only via `kotoba-lang/perfgate`, this kernel, min quantile, 25 rotated
  samples.

Do not land fused-srem, extra MOV peepholes, FMA, PGO, a kototama optimizer,
or a timed `bench` export. Do not claim LLVM beaten. Do not overwrite
iterations 04–08."}]
